.Dd July 28, 2026
.Dt FUSE-UFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fuse-ufs
.Nd FUSE implementation of FreeBSD's UFSv2
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fqv
.Op Fl o Ar option[,option...]
.Ar special
.Ar mountpoint
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a FUSE implementation of FreeBSD's UFSv2 filesystem.
It mounts UFSv2 filesystem images and block devices read-only by default;
experimental read-write access is available via the
.Cm rw
option.
.Pp
Both little- and big-endian filesystems are supported, regardless of the host's
native byte order.
.Nm
selects a FUSE backend at compile time:
.Cm fuse3
.Pq via Xr fuser Ns -based libraries, used on Linux and FreeBSD
or
.Cm fuse2
.Pq via fuse2rs, used on OpenBSD .
.Pp
Permission checking with
.Cm default_permissions
is always in effect: access checks are performed by the kernel using the
credentials of the calling process.
.Pp
The following command-line options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground and wait for the filesystem to be unmounted before
exiting.
.It Fl o Ar option[,option...]
Comma-separated list of mount options; see
.Sx Mount options
below.
Unknown options are passed through to the FUSE backend.
.It Fl q
Decrease logging verbosity.
.It Fl v
Increase logging verbosity; may be given more than once.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a help message and exit.
.It Fl V , -version
Print version information and exit.
.El
.Ss Mount options
Mount options are supplied as a comma-separated list to
.Fl o .
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm allow_other
Allow other users to access the mounted filesystem.
.It Cm allow_root
Allow the root user to access the mounted filesystem.
.Pq fuse3 backend only.
.It Cm async
Perform filesystem updates asynchronously.
.It Cm atime
Update file access times
.Pq the default .
.It Cm auto_unmount
Automatically unmount the filesystem if the calling process exits.
.Pq fuse3 backend only.
.It Cm default_permissions
No effect: kernel permission checks are always enabled.
.It Cm dev | nodev
Allow or prohibit access to devices on the mounted filesystem.
.It Cm dirsync
Synchronize directory updates.
.Pq fuse3 backend only.
.It Cm exec | noexec
Allow or prohibit execution of programs from the mounted filesystem.
.It Cm noatime
Do not update file access times.
.It Cm ro
Mount the filesystem read-only.
This is the default.
.It Cm rw
Mount the filesystem read-write.
Write support is
.Em experimental
and may corrupt data; use with caution.
.It Cm suid | nosuid
Honor or ignore the set-user-ID and set-group-ID bits when executing programs
from the mounted filesystem.
.It Cm sync
Perform filesystem updates synchronously.
.It Cm debug
Enable FUSE backend debug output.
.Pq fuse2 backend only.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount
.Pa /dev/sda1
read-only onto
.Pa /mnt :
.Pp
.Dl $ fuse-ufs /dev/sda1 /mnt
.Pp
The same, but allow other users to access the mounted filesystem:
.Pp
.Dl $ fuse-ufs -o allow_other /dev/sda1 /mnt
.Pp
Mount with experimental read-write access and verbose logging:
.Pp
.Dl $ fuse-ufs -fv -o rw /dev/sda1 /mnt
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs 8
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/realchonk/fuse-ufs
